			"Message": "feat(Common): Add W3C traceparent builder for cross-tier distributed tracing\n\nExtend the `Telemetry` module in Common with a new `Traceparent` component to standardize distributed context propagation across tier boundaries (Mountain ↔ Cocoon, Mountain ↔ Sky, Sidecars). Implement `Build` and `Parse` functions for W3C version-00 `traceparent` headers, ensuring every process maintains a stable `TraceId` while minting unique `SpanId` values for each inter-process call.\n\nThis addition unifies the observability surface by allowing OTLP and PostHog events to share a consistent trace identity, enabling end-to-end tracing from the editor UI through the native backend and into the extension host. The implementation derives the trace ID deterministically from the process ID and current nanosecond timestamp to ensure agreement between the OTLP exporter and the header builder, even across separate modules.",
			"SHA": "490bcfbfeb03025ac7e8a7c0c4127b1bc32bd077"
		}
